  "notes": "- **Security fix for CVE-2026-111497.** The Brotli decompression library the\n  browser uses to unpack web pages could be made to write past the end of its\n  memory by a malicious server. This update brings the fixed library\n  (Debian's 1.1.0-2+deb13u1) through the normal software update, without an\n  operating system update, and the browser restarts in the maintenance\n  window to start using it. Once a display gets an operating system update\n  that already contains the fix, this copy removes itself.",
